<p>Responsive image styles need Drupal breakpoints. The plugin writes them to <code>dist/&lt;theme&gt;_dist.breakpoints.yml</code>, one per Tailwind screen plus an <code>xs</code> breakpoint without a media query.</p>

<h2>Generated for this theme</h2>
{% include code_block with { lang: 'yaml', title: generated.breakpoints.path, code: generated.breakpoints.code } only %}

<h2>Multipliers</h2>
<p>Every breakpoint gets the same multipliers. The default is <code>1x</code> and <code>2x</code>:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'ts', title: 'vite.config.ts' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
uebertool({
  breakpoints: {
    multipliers: ['1x', '2x', '3x'],
  },
})
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

{% embed aside with { type: 'caution', title: 'Default Tailwind screens only' } %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>The breakpoints come from Tailwind's <em>default</em> theme (<code>tailwindcss/defaultTheme</code>), not from your stylesheet. Custom <code>--breakpoint-*</code> values in your CSS <code>@theme</code> are not picked up.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

<p>The breakpoint group is called <code>&lt;theme&gt; Tailwind</code> and shows up in the responsive image style form.</p>
